But they decided to get going when they had something that was really useful.

111
00:05:49,890 --> 00:05:53,467
这是他们第一张实体卡的样子。在有这张卡之前
This is how their first physical card looked like this. Before they had this card,

112
00:05:53,467 --> 00:05:54,730
他们只有一张虚拟卡
they just had a virtual card.

113
00:05:55,210 --> 00:05:58,212
Brex 联系了他们的 YC 批次同学和其他 YC 公司
Brex reach out to them, their YC batch and other YC companies

114
00:05:58,212 --> 00:06:00,050
这是他们发出的邮件
and this is the email that they sent.

115
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,800
我就读其中一小段
I'm just gonna read a brief portion of it.

116
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:07,960
嘿，各位，我们为 winter 17 批次的朋友开放内测，有 10 个内测名额
Hey guys, we're opening up a beta for winter 17 batch friends with 10 spots for beta users.

117
00:06:08,200 --> 00:06:10,760
10 个名额。听起来名额有限，所以我该赶紧行动
10 spots. That sounds like there's a limited spot. So I should take actions.

118
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:15,560
Brex 是一张专注于科技公司的企业信用卡。那说的就是我，完美
Brex is a corporate credit card focused on technology companies. That's me. Perfect.

119
00:06:15,640 --> 00:06:18,878
你其实是直接针对你的客户来写这封邮件
You're actually writing the email directly towards your customers.

120
00:06:18,878 --> 00:06:20,720
我们不需要个人担保
We don't require a personal guarantee.

121
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:22,840
它能为刚起步的初创公司提供授信。
It can underwrite startups who just got started.

122
00:06:23,390 --> 00:06:28,230
这就是它的价值主张。Brex 的大多数其他替代品都没有这样的东西。
This was the value prop. Most other alternatives to Brex did not have something like this.

123
00:06:28,390 --> 00:06:30,030
那要多少钱呢？免费。
So how much does it cost? It's free.

124
00:06:30,550 --> 00:06:33,270
商家在付钱给我们，所以没有年费。
The merchants are paying us. So there's zero annual fees.

125
00:06:33,270 --> 00:06:34,630
这看起来是显而易见的选择。
This seems like a no brainer.

126
00:06:34,790 --> 00:06:38,430
我觉得这封邮件可能有点太长了，但它确实奏效了。
I would argue that this email is probably a little bit too long, but it did work.

127
00:06:38,790 --> 00:06:41,950
